# The same zip's PKV.rsp (public key validation), all 12 of its [P-384]
# section in order: the result and its reason as NIST writes them - P (0),
# F (1, Q_x or Q_y out of range), F (2, point not on curve) - then Qx, Qy.
# Every out-of-range coordinate here is 97 hex digits, 2^384 or more: no
# 97-byte encoding holds it, so it is written at its own width (49 bytes)
# and refused for its length.
